                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7ab37a59-7107-4a5c-adef-db8a4ad0229b",
                        "entry_id": "47468d08-efbd-3898-9af9-0e471738b814",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "auto-sacrifices"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3e4c594e-8b80-3fce-9d47-e610b6eeea40",
                        "entry_id": "47468d08-efbd-3898-9af9-0e471738b814",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sacrifice, plus ou moins consenti et volontaire, de soi-même."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccf53b6a-2b93-4059-8b2e-887586691107",
                                "sense_id": "3e4c594e-8b80-3fce-9d47-e610b6eeea40",
                                "text": "En relation avec les mythes sur l’origine des métaux, on rencontrera des complexes mythico-rituels embrassant la notion de la genèse par le sacrifice ou l’auto-sacrifice d’un dieu, les rapports entre la mystique agricole, la métallurgie et l’alchimie, enfin les idées de croissance naturelle, croissance précipitée et « perfection »."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "05831eb8-1cd2-3bfe-a0f0-e5e5919fddab",
                        "entry_id": "47468d08-efbd-3898-9af9-0e471738b814",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Renoncement à ses intérêts propres, abnégation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2d88b7f2-ca7b-4b62-8d1f-de7fddfeab80",
                        "source_entry_id": "47468d08-efbd-3898-9af9-0e471738b814",
                        "source_sense_description": "Religion",
                        "target_lang_word": "self-sacrifice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "self-sacrifice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79198f33-1a2c-39f3-9e3e-780d4aae7f98",
                                        "entry_id": "51987232-abf5-321a-a9e6-727c040ec636",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The giving up of one's own benefit for the good of others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d28bd59c-c94f-46d5-9679-0339bcf86f29",
                                                "sense_id": "79198f33-1a2c-39f3-9e3e-780d4aae7f98",
                                                "text": "Caring for a loved one with a chronic illness inevitably involves self-sacrifice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f1f06df-4412-4450-8b86-2e3974f307da",
                                                "sense_id": "79198f33-1a2c-39f3-9e3e-780d4aae7f98",
                                                "text": "Whatever he was suffering, it was she who had caused it; he had vacated his house on account of her. She was not worth such self-sacrifice; she should not have accepted it of him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17f8183c-0a0d-48cb-98c2-160a3f2eafff",
                                                "sense_id": "79198f33-1a2c-39f3-9e3e-780d4aae7f98",
                                                "text": "Some of those boys came straight from the cornfields with only a summer’s wages in their pockets, hung on through the four years, shabby and underfed, and completed the course by really heroic self-sacrifice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8f99baa-ae80-4861-ab20-9dc83f636d99",
                                                "sense_id": "79198f33-1a2c-39f3-9e3e-780d4aae7f98",
                                                "text": "Turians have a strong inclination towards public service and self-sacrifice, so they tend to be poor entrepreneurs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7cf0ae8-47bd-461c-9493-bf2c9debdc17",
                                                "sense_id": "79198f33-1a2c-39f3-9e3e-780d4aae7f98",
                                                "text": "[…] he turned his resourceful mind away from the serene life of a don on grass lawns in Cambridge to one of self-sacrifice and pure devotion in the thorny bushes of Africa."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f221387c-cdaa-307e-9f0d-599a515196c1",
                                        "entry_id": "51987232-abf5-321a-a9e6-727c040ec636",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of making the ultimate sacrifice of giving up one's life for a cause."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d43f1e6-ec85-4987-93f2-305b28217e44",
                                                "sense_id": "f221387c-cdaa-307e-9f0d-599a515196c1",
                                                "text": "His brave self-sacrifice won him a posthumous medal, but I think he'd have preferred to receive it in person."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10f77ead-3877-4cb7-ae73-50bb691caad3",
                                                "sense_id": "f221387c-cdaa-307e-9f0d-599a515196c1",
                                                "text": "[Scott’s Last Expedition] had been one of my own favourite books. It seemed curiously dated now, this heroism with only the ice for enemy, self-sacrifice that involved no deaths beyond one’s own."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f4805aa-aaa6-4ae4-986e-62672ebaf1e4",
                                                "sense_id": "f221387c-cdaa-307e-9f0d-599a515196c1",
                                                "text": "However, something once happened on the railway there which showed the very best of mankind: heroism, duty, self-sacrifice and calm professionalism under terrible pressure. It is a story which gives us far, far better reasons for remembering this attractive little town, which without these heroes would have been blown to smithereens in a gigantic explosion. (Two railwaymen lost their lives in 1944 when a wagon in an ammunition train caught fire and blew up, an even worse disaster was averted however.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
